# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTHZ - NOT-FOUND MATRIX: CATALOG AND QUOTES (NON-EXISTENT ROUTE IDS, ADMIN-ACCOUNT SESSION)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Part of the not-found matrix, split by resource for the 250-line test file limit: parts, labor types and quotes incl. quote lines (customers, vehicles and appointments live in not-found-matrix-customers.http).
# Every mutation endpoint that takes a route id, called with a non-existent
# id (999999). Each must answer 404, never 500. A plain mechanic session is
# enough for all of them: Customers/Vehicles/Appointments require only an
# authenticated session (no Customer person ever gets an IdentityUserId, so
# every session is a mechanic session, see catalog-authz.http), and
# Parts/LaborTypes/Quotes are MechanicOnly. AdminOnly appointment
# assign/unassign (PUT and DELETE /api/appointments/{id}/assign/{mechanicId})
# would 403 under a mechanic session before reaching a not-found check, so
# they are excluded here; their not-found cases (appointment_not_found,
# mechanic_not_found) are already covered under an admin session in
# tests/API/appointments/admin-assign-unassign.http.
# Signs in with the admin account: the admin is a mechanic person too (person_type mechanic), so it
# passes MechanicOnly, and nothing in this file depends on the Admin role.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@SessionEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@SessionPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@RunId = {{$timestamp}}
@NonExistentId = 999999
@GhostVin = TST{{RunId.toString().slice(-10)}}0401


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Setup][Authz] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Authz] Login with the admin account (200 expected)
# @name csrfSource1
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{SessionEmail}}",
  "password": "{{SessionPassword}}"
}

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('autoservice_csrf='))?.match(/^autoservice_csrf=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

# ── Catalog: Parts (Catalog/PartEndpoints*.cs) ────────────────


### [Negative][Authz] PUT /api/parts/{{NonExistentId}} (404 expected)
PUT {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/parts/{{NonExistentId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partNumber": "GHOST-PART", "name": "Ghost", "netUnitPrice": 100, "vatRatePercent": 27 }

?? status == 404

###

### [Negative][Authz] DELETE /api/parts/{{NonExistentId}} (404 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/parts/{{NonExistentId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 404

###

# ── Catalog: Labor Types (Catalog/LaborTypeEndpoints*.cs) ─────


### [Negative][Authz] PUT /api/labor-types/{{NonExistentId}} (404 expected)
PUT {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/labor-types/{{NonExistentId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "GHOST-LT", "name": "Ghost", "hourlyNetRate": 100, "vatRatePercent": 27 }

?? status == 404

###

### [Negative][Authz] DELETE /api/labor-types/{{NonExistentId}} (404 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/labor-types/{{NonExistentId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 404

###

